A||||10||JBGehling||85 GT Question...||||1||
Z||000000||JBGehling||12-02-2000||11:25 PM||||I have just recently found myself admiring the notchback on the 85 GT (I thought I was pure fastback, but the 85 GT's do look damn neat-o  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)! I was wondering if you Fiero purists could help me out here:<P>1) was the 85 GT notchback only offered in 1985, or were the 1986-87 SE's the same?<P>Also, could you post pictures of your 85 GT (if you have one).<P>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000001||82-T/A||12-02-2000||11:35 PM||||The first year the Fiero GT was introduced was in 1985. In 1985, ALL Fieros were notchback. The Fastback design was new in 1986.<P>The 86-87 SEs are exactly the same car.. well, they're all the same cars.. but the 86-87 SEs and 85 GTs are even more so of the same car.<P><BR>The 85 GT, IMHO is one of the BEST Fieros you can buy. It's got the most HP of them all, (rated differently, but it's still a tad quicker). It's got the highest gear ratio, the highest fuel pressure, and among other things, all 85 GTs came with WS6, where as afterwards.. it was just an option in the GTs.<P>I had a 1985 Fiero GT.. but I don't have any more pictures of it.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||12-02-2000||11:49 PM||||T/A's correct. The 85 Gt and the 86/87 Se's were pretty much the same. I love the 85 Gt's as well. The ONLY thing I dont like about the 85's is that they dont have the aux guage cluster over the radio pod...but no biggie.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rodmcneill||12-03-2000||12:08 AM||||Do the 85 GTs come with a 85 or a 120 mph speedo? I thought all 86-88 GTs came with the WS6 handling pkg. as standard equipment. ||||reg||5
Z||000004||2xsess||12-03-2000||01:57 AM||||Ok, here's my opinion, I've had an 86Gt and an 88GT t-top and I currently have an 85GT. I loved my 88GT,of course, it was the first one I had totally rebuilt and saved from the scrap heap. <BR>One major plus is that it is so much easier to work on the engines in the notchbacks, you don't have to do yoga to get around the rear clip like the fastbacks.<P>rodmcneill, the 85GTs come with the 85mph speedo, the 86-87 SEs have the 120 I think<P>Here's a pic of my 85GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)_1.jpg"> <BR>Here's an 86SE<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/red86se.jpg"> <BR>Here's a good comparision pic RobertVols stock 88GT and Turbo86SE's sweet ride  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLmeet.jpg"> <P>I'm not saying that I don't love the looks of the fastback, one day I'll have another 88GT for sure  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> but I'll still be holding on to my 85GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Jeff<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||12-03-2000||02:17 AM||||WS6 was standard in <B>all</B> GT's.  Slightly stiffer springs and differently valved shocks is about all it is.  It was an option on SE's, and not available on coupes.  Also standard on the Formula.  Doesn't really make that much of a difference after 12-15 years, since the shocks need replacing anyways, and shock technology has come a ways since then.  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||onfire||12-03-2000||02:28 AM||||Here are a few pictures of the 85 GT I used to own.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/files/SIDE.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/files/REAR.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>"I seen it on the internet, and I believe everthing on the net."<BR><A HREF="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/on_fire.html" TARGET=_blank>Check out my waist of banbwidth.</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-03-2000||01:22 PM||||Personally, I prefer the notchbacks (which would explain why I have an '86 coupe, an '85 GT and have another '85 GT on the way).  I think it basically comes down to this:  the notchbacks look more muscular than sporty, and the fastbacks look more sporty than muscular.  Since I like the muscle car look, I chose the notchback.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Carrolles||12-03-2000||01:36 PM||||Although the 86 and 87 SEs have the same notchback as the 85GT I don't believe they have the same ground effects/rocker panels.<P>I believe 86 and 87 SEs have 85mph backlit speedometers and can also have the aux gauge set.  I think just the 86 through 88GTs and the Formula have the 120 mph speedometer.<P>I got an instrument cluster including aux. gauges from an 86SE and it is an 85mph speedometer and is backlit.  I'm going to put it in my 85SE v-6.  My 85GT has the dimly lit 85mph cluster just like my 85SE.<P>I personaly like the notchback better than the fastback because it is more unique to Fieros.  Too many cars have mimicked the Fiero fastback styling for my taste.  That's not saying that I'd turn down an 86/88 GT.  I'd take one in a heartbeat.<p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||12-03-2000||06:53 PM||||All 85 GT's and 86-87 SE/GT's and 88 GT's have the exact same rocker panels/ground fx, except that 86 and up have the rounded molding.<P>I think all 87 SE's and a very few late 86 SE's have 120 speedo's.  Not completly sure, tho.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||TJ's85gt||12-04-2000||03:28 PM||||  My car is an 85 GT and its got an 85mph speedo and i hit that tached out in third gear. My cars got 159,000 miles and runs strong. no rebuilds yet. still beats most older stangs and Z-28s. Only been beat by a tubo indy fiero, modified I-roc, freinds 90 mustang 5.0, and a red and white viper rt-10.                                                                                                crashed into an apt. building and an 82 volvo at 40 mph and still drivable!<P>------------------<BR>white 85 gt||||reg||1
